WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.733 position:59% line:85%
I've condensed seven years of lighting

00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:03.433 line:85%
experience into one video.

00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:04.833 position:56% line:85%
I'm going to show you how to light a

00:00:04.833 --> 00:00:06.233 line:85%
product in Blender beautifully

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.433 line:85%
and it can apply to

00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:08.633 line:85%
most other 3D software.

00:00:08.966 --> 00:00:09.966 line:85%
Right, let's get started.

00:00:11.199 --> 00:00:13.466 position:59% line:85%
All right, so let's first add a plane,

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:14.766 line:85%
make sure it's in the center

00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:17.866 position:64% line:85%
and go to view, cameras, active camera to

00:00:17.866 --> 00:00:18.600 line:85%
look through the camera.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.199 line:85%
And also if you have the

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:21.333 line:85%
3D cursor in the middle here

00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:22.800 line:85%
and in the transform people

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.899 line:85%
point you have it selected.

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:26.266 line:85%
When we then rotate, we will rotate

00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:27.466 line:85%
around the middle of the scene.

00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:29.133 position:59% line:85%
This is much easier to move the camera

00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:30.833 position:64% line:85%
because then we will be always looking at

00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:31.699 line:85%
the center of the screen.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:32.966 line:85%
And let's also go

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:33.833 line:85%
into the camera settings

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.133 line:85%
and change the focal

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.766 line:85%
length to 120 millimeters.

00:00:37.066 --> 00:00:38.466 position:59% line:85%
This is because we don't want too much

00:00:38.466 --> 00:00:39.799 line:85%
distortion on the lens

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.666 line:85%
when taking pictures of products

00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:42.833 position:56% line:85%
because we want to show the products

00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:43.833 line:85%
exactly how they look.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.466 line:85%
Let's scale this scene up.

00:00:45.466 --> 00:00:47.033 line:85%
We can also rotate the

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:47.833 line:85%
camera a little bit down.

00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:49.066 line:85%
I think this looks good.

00:00:49.066 --> 00:00:49.733 line:85%
All right, so we need

00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:50.766 line:85%
something to actually light.

00:00:50.966 --> 00:00:52.733 line:85%
So let's add a sphere in the start.

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.133 line:85%
We'll start simple with a sphere

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:55.533 line:85%
and then we'll move on to

00:00:55.533 --> 00:00:56.966 line:85%
actual product very soon.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.066 line:85%
Also shade smooth this sphere.

00:00:59.466 --> 00:01:00.366 line:85%
Then let's turn on the

00:01:00.366 --> 00:01:01.799 line:85%
render preview like this.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:02.666 line:85%
And let's start with

00:01:02.666 --> 00:01:03.733 position:58% line:85%
something you might have heard about,

00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:04.833 line:85%
the three point lighting.

00:01:05.266 --> 00:01:06.799 position:59% line:85%
So for this first we need a key light.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.233 line:85%
So let's add a area light.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.400 position:64% line:85%
And again, change the point to 3D cursor.

00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:11.933 line:85%
And if you rotate now, it

00:01:11.933 --> 00:01:13.200 line:85%
will rotate around the scene,

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.133 line:85%
which is very useful.

00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:15.533 line:85%
And for the key light will

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:17.166 line:85%
be the most important light.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.666 position:61% line:85%
So I like to put this in front and then

00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:20.633 line:85%
tilt it a little bit.

00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:22.333 position:61% line:85%
Think we can also move it further away.

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:24.333 line:85%
I think this is a good location.

00:01:24.966 --> 00:01:26.433 line:85%
Okay, so one issue now is

00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:27.533 line:85%
that you see the shadows here.

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:29.233 position:56% line:85%
They might be a little bit too dark,

00:01:29.233 --> 00:01:30.533 line:85%
especially the shadow behind here.

00:01:30.866 --> 00:01:31.733 line:85%
And the way we often fix

00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:33.400 line:85%
that with is with a fill light.

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:35.133 position:56% line:85%
But this doesn't need to be a light.

00:01:35.433 --> 00:01:37.433 line:85%
I like to use a plane instead.

00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:39.166 position:59% line:85%
So let's add a plane, scale this down.

00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:41.200 line:85%
And let's place this on the

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.366 line:85%
side of the sphere like this.

00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:43.533 line:85%
And of course, we don't

00:01:43.533 --> 00:01:44.333 line:85%
want to see this plane.

00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:45.766 line:85%
So go into object properties

00:01:45.766 --> 00:01:47.333 line:85%
and scroll down to visibility

00:01:47.766 --> 00:01:51.033 line:85%
and disable the camera and shadow.

00:01:51.433 --> 00:01:52.066 line:85%
So now we basically

00:01:52.066 --> 00:01:53.566 line:85%
have a invisible plane here

00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:56.066 position:64% line:85%
that reflects this light onto the sphere.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.099 position:64% line:85%
And what this does is that it softens out

00:01:59.099 --> 00:02:00.166 line:85%
this shadow a little bit.

00:02:00.166 --> 00:02:01.066 line:85%
So if you hide this plane

00:02:01.066 --> 00:02:02.366 line:85%
now, we'll see it's very dark.

00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:04.633 position:63% line:85%
And if we unhide it, we will see that we

00:02:04.633 --> 00:02:07.066 line:85%
have a nice soft shadow here.

00:02:07.366 --> 00:02:08.033 line:85%
And if you see here, we

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.266 line:85%
have an ugly line here.

00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:10.333 line:85%
So to fix this, let's

00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:11.366 line:85%
just move it up a little bit.

00:02:11.733 --> 00:02:12.266 line:85%
I think this is good.

00:02:12.566 --> 00:02:13.533 line:85%
And for the last light,

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.133 line:85%
let's add a backlight.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.733 position:63% line:85%
And that is exactly what it sounds like.

00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:18.300 line:85%
It's a light we put behind the

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.233 line:85%
object to add some backlight.

00:02:20.566 --> 00:02:21.833 position:59% line:85%
And of course, we don't want this ugly

00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:23.033 line:85%
light on the floor here.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:24.900 line:85%
So to fix this, go into object

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.766 line:85%
properties, scroll down to shading.

00:02:27.166 --> 00:02:28.933 line:85%
Under light linking, press new.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.233 line:85%
And let's drag the floor

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:32.033 line:85%
object into the light leaking here

00:02:32.166 --> 00:02:33.433 line:85%
and disable this check mark.

00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:35.666 position:61% line:85%
Now it will not light up the floor, but

00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:36.866 line:85%
it will light up the sphere.

00:02:37.266 --> 00:02:38.333 line:85%
And the point of the backlight is

00:02:38.333 --> 00:02:39.800 line:85%
basically to add a nice

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.800 line:85%
rim light around the subject.

00:02:43.966 --> 00:02:44.633 line:85%
And if you're enjoying the

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:45.733 line:85%
video, make sure to subscribe.

00:02:45.933 --> 00:02:47.199 line:85%
And if you have a suggestion for a

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:48.699 position:58% line:85%
tutorial, make sure to comment below.

00:02:49.099 --> 00:02:50.599 position:56% line:85%
I read every single comment and your

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:51.733 line:85%
suggestions are amazing.

00:02:51.766 --> 00:02:52.933 line:85%
So thanks for that.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:54.833 line:85%
All right. On with the video.

00:02:55.199 --> 00:02:56.800 line:85%
All right. So we just lit a sphere.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.033 position:58% line:85%
So what do you think the next one is?

00:02:58.033 --> 00:02:59.166 line:85%
And it's a default cube.

00:02:59.166 --> 00:02:59.800 line:85%
So of course, we have

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:00.599 line:85%
to delete this later.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.533 line:85%
So let's just put a cube in here.

00:03:02.933 --> 00:03:03.966 line:85%
Now let's add a light and

00:03:03.966 --> 00:03:05.366 line:85%
you might spot some problems.

00:03:05.366 --> 00:03:06.033 line:85%
Problem is that the

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.366 line:85%
edges are way too sharp

00:03:07.533 --> 00:03:08.633 line:85%
and the surfaces are

00:03:08.633 --> 00:03:09.933 line:85%
way too flat and boring.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.266 line:85%
And a way to improve

00:03:11.266 --> 00:03:12.800 line:85%
this is to add some bevels.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.566 position:61% line:85%
And we have two ways of improving this.

00:03:14.866 --> 00:03:16.466 position:56% line:85%
The one way is to do it in material.

00:03:16.766 --> 00:03:18.099 line:85%
So let's add a new material.

00:03:18.266 --> 00:03:19.300 line:85%
Let's also make it metallic

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.633 line:85%
because then it's easier to see.

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:22.099 position:58% line:85%
Turn the roughness down a little bit.

00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:23.833 line:85%
And let's add a bevel node.

00:03:24.166 --> 00:03:25.866 position:64% line:85%
And when we connect this into the normal,

00:03:25.866 --> 00:03:27.433 position:59% line:85%
you will see that the edges soften up,

00:03:27.433 --> 00:03:29.033 position:59% line:85%
but it's kind of too strong right now.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.466 position:59% line:85%
So let's turn the radius down to 0.02.

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:32.699 line:85%
Think that's nice.

00:03:33.066 --> 00:03:34.333 line:85%
And already, if we now try

00:03:34.333 --> 00:03:35.166 line:85%
to move the light around,

00:03:35.466 --> 00:03:37.033 line:85%
we get some nice edges here.

00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:38.300 line:85%
And that already makes the

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.233 line:85%
cube look more realistic.

00:03:39.666 --> 00:03:40.666 line:85%
But there are some issues.

00:03:40.666 --> 00:03:41.966 line:85%
If we zoom in, we will

00:03:41.966 --> 00:03:43.266 line:85%
still see the original edge

00:03:43.266 --> 00:03:44.866 position:58% line:85%
because this is only happening in the

00:03:44.866 --> 00:03:46.233 line:85%
shader, not in the mesh itself.

00:03:46.566 --> 00:03:48.466 line:85%
So the best way to add bevels is of

00:03:48.466 --> 00:03:49.599 line:85%
course, do it manually.

00:03:49.866 --> 00:03:51.133 line:85%
So let's remove this bevel

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:52.466 line:85%
shader and go into modifiers.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.166 line:85%
And let's add a bevel modifier.

00:03:55.433 --> 00:03:56.233 line:85%
Let's do five segments

00:03:56.233 --> 00:03:58.833 line:85%
and let's make it 0.03.

00:03:59.433 --> 00:04:00.466 line:85%
So now our bevels are

00:04:00.466 --> 00:04:01.333 line:85%
much higher quality.

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:02.066 line:85%
And you can see it

00:04:02.066 --> 00:04:03.133 line:85%
already looks more realistic.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.500 position:56% line:85%
All right, let's move on to actually

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.500 line:85%
lighting a real product.

00:04:05.933 --> 00:04:06.666 line:85%
And of course, if you

00:04:06.666 --> 00:04:07.466 line:85%
want this blender file,

00:04:07.533 --> 00:04:08.633 line:85%
go to my Patreon and

00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:09.900 line:85%
you can get it over there.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.466 position:63% line:85%
There you will also get all the assets I

00:04:11.466 --> 00:04:12.233 line:85%
used in this tutorial.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:13.933 position:59% line:85%
All right, so let's start with a three

00:04:13.933 --> 00:04:15.066 line:85%
point lighting on this one.

00:04:15.333 --> 00:04:17.333 line:85%
So as before, add a key light.

00:04:17.366 --> 00:04:19.433 line:85%
You can also make this a

00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:20.633 line:85%
bit stronger, maybe 25.

00:04:20.966 --> 00:04:21.766 line:85%
And when we have a nice

00:04:21.766 --> 00:04:23.033 line:85%
key light, let's add a fill.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.633 line:85%
So add a plane like before.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:27.100 line:85%
Let's place this in front

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.733 line:85%
of the object like this.

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.333 line:85%
Let's also go into object

00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:31.699 line:85%
properties and go into visibility,

00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:33.066 line:85%
turn off camera and

00:04:33.066 --> 00:04:34.133 line:85%
shadow so it's invisible.

00:04:34.466 --> 00:04:36.033 position:64% line:85%
Now we have softened up the shadows here.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.966 line:85%
And let's also make the backlight.

00:04:38.199 --> 00:04:39.166 line:85%
So let's duplicate this

00:04:39.166 --> 00:04:40.766 line:85%
and let's rotate it around.

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.600 position:64% line:85%
And I like to move the light around until

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.866 line:85%
I find the perfect spot.

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.133 line:85%
For example, here, if

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:46.133 line:85%
you look at the top here,

00:04:46.166 --> 00:04:48.366 position:64% line:85%
I don't want it to be flat and all white.

00:04:48.766 --> 00:04:49.266 line:85%
So if you move it

00:04:49.266 --> 00:04:50.833 line:85%
slightly more, rotate it,

00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:52.733 position:58% line:85%
we can get a nice gradient like this.

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:54.066 line:85%
And I think this looks nice.

00:04:54.366 --> 00:04:54.866 line:85%
Of course, we don't

00:04:54.866 --> 00:04:55.933 line:85%
want it to be bright here.

00:04:55.933 --> 00:04:56.933 line:85%
So like before, let's go

00:04:56.933 --> 00:04:57.899 line:85%
into object properties.

00:04:58.233 --> 00:04:59.466 line:85%
On light linking, click new.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:01.233 position:61% line:85%
And let's drag the floor into the light

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:02.966 line:85%
linking and disable the check mark.

00:05:03.433 --> 00:05:04.133 line:85%
And I think we can make

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:05.066 line:85%
this a little bit weaker.

00:05:05.066 --> 00:05:06.133 line:85%
So let's do five.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.800 position:64% line:85%
So imagine you're making a teaser and you

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:10.966 position:59% line:85%
don't want to show the entire product.

00:05:11.266 --> 00:05:13.333 position:64% line:85%
Then I like to only work with backlights.

00:05:13.366 --> 00:05:15.133 line:85%
So let's add a light and

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:17.399 line:85%
let's put it behind the product.

00:05:17.733 --> 00:05:19.733 position:61% line:85%
And again, let's also add a light group

00:05:19.733 --> 00:05:20.666 line:85%
and drag the floor

00:05:20.666 --> 00:05:21.933 line:85%
into it and disable it.

00:05:21.966 --> 00:05:24.033 line:85%
So it doesn't light up the floor.

00:05:24.433 --> 00:05:25.766 line:85%
And I think this looks nice.

00:05:25.766 --> 00:05:27.266 line:85%
We can also duplicate

00:05:27.266 --> 00:05:29.300 line:85%
this light with shift D

00:05:29.433 --> 00:05:31.399 position:59% line:85%
and then rotate one to the other side.

00:05:31.699 --> 00:05:33.333 position:59% line:85%
Make sure it's more or less symmetric.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:34.500 line:85%
And now we have a pretty

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.899 line:85%
cool teaser for a product.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:36.899 line:85%
Alright, for this one, we're

00:05:36.899 --> 00:05:38.233 line:85%
lighting it for e-commerce,

00:05:38.233 --> 00:05:39.066 line:85%
which is basically

00:05:39.066 --> 00:05:40.666 line:85%
product images for websites.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:41.833 line:85%
And they often have a

00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:42.800 line:85%
completely white background.

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.600 line:85%
So let's try to light it like that.

00:05:44.866 --> 00:05:47.699 position:56% line:85%
So add a light and let's move it up.

00:05:47.699 --> 00:05:50.366 position:64% line:85%
Let's make this larger and pretty strong.

00:05:50.699 --> 00:05:51.333 line:85%
I think that looks nice.

00:05:51.766 --> 00:05:53.533 line:85%
And I also like to duplicate it.

00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:55.233 line:85%
So shift D to duplicate it.

00:05:55.233 --> 00:05:56.399 line:85%
And for the second one,

00:05:56.399 --> 00:05:57.266 line:85%
let's make it really small.

00:05:57.566 --> 00:05:58.733 line:85%
And let's make this weaker.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.366 line:85%
This is just to add a

00:06:00.366 --> 00:06:01.966 line:85%
nice specular like this.

00:06:01.966 --> 00:06:03.666 position:61% line:85%
Because if you just have a large light,

00:06:03.866 --> 00:06:04.800 line:85%
we won't get any

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.233 line:85%
reflections because it's too large.

00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:07.766 position:61% line:85%
If you have a small one, it's easier to

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:08.633 line:85%
see the reflections.

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:09.666 line:85%
And we also want to

00:06:09.666 --> 00:06:10.766 line:85%
make our background white.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.933 position:63% line:85%
So let's disable render preview for now.

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:14.033 line:85%
Let's take the floor,

00:06:14.433 --> 00:06:15.366 line:85%
make it much smaller.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.166 line:85%
I think this is good.

00:06:16.566 --> 00:06:18.633 position:63% line:85%
And go into edit mode, select this edge.

00:06:18.966 --> 00:06:20.333 line:85%
Let's extrude it up with E.

00:06:20.666 --> 00:06:21.833 line:85%
Let's select this edge

00:06:21.833 --> 00:06:24.133 line:85%
here and Ctrl B to bevel it.

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:24.899 line:85%
Let's bevel it like

00:06:24.899 --> 00:06:26.533 line:85%
this, scroll up to add detail

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.800 position:59% line:85%
and also make sure it's shaded smooth.

00:06:29.066 --> 00:06:31.566 position:63% line:85%
And that it covers the entire area here.

00:06:31.566 --> 00:06:33.133 line:85%
And if you go into render mode now,

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:34.133 line:85%
we have a white background,

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:35.466 line:85%
but we want to make it a bit wider.

00:06:35.766 --> 00:06:39.166 position:63% line:85%
So let's also pop this light and make it

00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:39.766 line:85%
a little bit smaller

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.066 line:85%
and put it behind.

00:06:41.433 --> 00:06:42.766 line:85%
So if you click render now,

00:06:42.866 --> 00:06:43.633 line:85%
we have a product

00:06:43.633 --> 00:06:45.233 line:85%
nicely lit for e-commerce.

00:06:45.666 --> 00:06:46.866 line:85%
And it's a little bit dark still,

00:06:46.866 --> 00:06:48.266 position:61% line:85%
so we can make this, I think, stronger.

00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:49.533 line:85%
And I think that looks nice.

00:06:50.133 --> 00:06:50.466 line:85%
All right.

00:06:50.466 --> 00:06:51.566 line:85%
So for the next one,

00:06:51.566 --> 00:06:52.733 line:85%
we're lighting glass.

00:06:52.966 --> 00:06:54.766 position:63% line:85%
And glass is often pretty hard to light.

00:06:55.166 --> 00:06:56.033 line:85%
Imagine you have a simple

00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:57.166 line:85%
lighting setup like this.

00:06:57.166 --> 00:06:57.966 line:85%
Then you want to show the

00:06:57.966 --> 00:06:58.933 line:85%
glass a little bit more.

00:06:58.933 --> 00:07:00.133 line:85%
So let's try lighting

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:01.433 line:85%
it up, add an air light.

00:07:01.866 --> 00:07:02.966 line:85%
Let's put it behind the glass.

00:07:02.966 --> 00:07:03.800 line:85%
And you'll probably see

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:04.800 line:85%
that it looks kind of ugly

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.333 line:85%
because it's completely white

00:07:06.466 --> 00:07:08.766 position:61% line:85%
and this edge is just completely sharp,

00:07:08.766 --> 00:07:09.800 line:85%
which doesn't really look nice.

00:07:10.133 --> 00:07:11.533 position:59% line:85%
So to fix this, go into the air light,

00:07:11.766 --> 00:07:13.666 position:58% line:85%
go into the shaders, click use nodes,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.600 line:85%
and let's add a gradient.

00:07:16.233 --> 00:07:17.266 line:85%
And let's add this one,

00:07:17.266 --> 00:07:18.699 line:85%
which we call elliptical sharper.

00:07:19.166 --> 00:07:20.466 position:56% line:85%
And you can make gradients like this

00:07:20.466 --> 00:07:22.366 line:85%
yourself in blender nodes.

00:07:22.366 --> 00:07:23.500 line:85%
But to keep it simple,

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.733 line:85%
I made them as textures.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.399 position:58% line:85%
You can also get them in the Patreon.

00:07:26.899 --> 00:07:27.933 line:85%
So let's connect this

00:07:27.933 --> 00:07:29.699 line:85%
into the emission color.

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:31.233 line:85%
And now let's move this

00:07:31.233 --> 00:07:32.933 line:85%
light behind the glass.

00:07:33.366 --> 00:07:34.666 line:85%
Let's rotate it down a little bit,

00:07:34.666 --> 00:07:36.300 line:85%
maybe take it a bit closer.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:37.533 line:85%
And the light already

00:07:37.533 --> 00:07:38.699 line:85%
looks much, much better.

00:07:39.233 --> 00:07:40.133 line:85%
Of course, this isn't

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:40.766 line:85%
physically accurate,

00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:42.033 line:85%
but it works really

00:07:42.033 --> 00:07:43.033 line:85%
well to make the glass

00:07:43.033 --> 00:07:44.766 line:85%
just look nicer and smoother.

00:07:45.166 --> 00:07:45.633 line:85%
You can also change

00:07:45.633 --> 00:07:46.300 line:85%
the color of the light

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:47.866 line:85%
to make it a bit more interesting.

00:07:48.899 --> 00:07:50.166 line:85%
All right, so for next one, we're

00:07:50.166 --> 00:07:51.933 line:85%
lighting a metallic object.

00:07:52.133 --> 00:07:53.199 line:85%
With metallic, it's very

00:07:53.199 --> 00:07:55.333 line:85%
similar to how we lit our glass.

00:07:55.666 --> 00:07:57.000 line:85%
So let's add a area light.

00:07:57.366 --> 00:07:58.133 line:85%
And we have the same

00:07:58.133 --> 00:07:59.600 line:85%
problem that it looks very ugly

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.033 position:56% line:85%
because the edges here are so sharp,

00:08:02.266 --> 00:08:03.933 position:61% line:85%
even when we put it in front like this.

00:08:03.933 --> 00:08:06.266 position:63% line:85%
So we have to go into the shader editor,

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.800 line:85%
click use nodes on the

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.366 line:85%
light, add our gradient.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.266 line:85%
And connect it into color.

00:08:13.766 --> 00:08:14.666 line:85%
And now we already have

00:08:14.666 --> 00:08:16.366 line:85%
much nicer looking light.

00:08:16.666 --> 00:08:17.666 line:85%
So I also like to

00:08:17.666 --> 00:08:19.833 line:85%
scale it up in the Z axis,

00:08:19.833 --> 00:08:21.566 position:63% line:85%
make it really tall, a little bit wider,

00:08:21.766 --> 00:08:22.933 line:85%
and also make it stronger.

00:08:23.399 --> 00:08:25.533 line:85%
And let's put two lights in the

00:08:25.533 --> 00:08:26.833 line:85%
background on each side.

00:08:27.199 --> 00:08:28.466 line:85%
And let's put two lights

00:08:28.466 --> 00:08:29.566 line:85%
in the front like this,

00:08:29.866 --> 00:08:30.566 line:85%
because we don't want

00:08:30.566 --> 00:08:32.000 line:85%
too much black areas

00:08:32.166 --> 00:08:34.433 line:85%
on our metal bottle like this.

00:08:34.666 --> 00:08:35.766 line:85%
And now we have lit a

00:08:35.766 --> 00:08:37.166 line:85%
pretty nice metallic object.

00:08:37.533 --> 00:08:39.566 position:64% line:85%
You can also use HRIs to add some detail.

00:08:39.766 --> 00:08:41.666 line:85%
But I try to use HRIs sparingly

00:08:41.666 --> 00:08:42.666 line:85%
because you don't have full

00:08:42.666 --> 00:08:43.733 line:85%
control over the lighting.

00:08:44.333 --> 00:08:45.033 line:85%
And with products, you

00:08:45.033 --> 00:08:46.299 line:85%
often want to have full control.

00:08:46.966 --> 00:08:47.833 line:85%
And for last one is

00:08:47.833 --> 00:08:49.533 line:85%
when to use a sunlight.

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:50.633 line:85%
Sometimes you have a

00:08:50.633 --> 00:08:52.733 line:85%
product with very flat colors

00:08:52.866 --> 00:08:54.166 line:85%
and matte surface.

00:08:54.633 --> 00:08:55.033 line:85%
And in these

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:56.066 line:85%
situations, you can't really play

00:08:56.066 --> 00:08:56.766 line:85%
with the reflections

00:08:56.766 --> 00:08:58.100 line:85%
and make it look nice.

00:08:58.466 --> 00:08:59.866 line:85%
And I often like to use sunlight.

00:09:00.266 --> 00:09:02.166 line:85%
So let's add a sunlight here.

00:09:02.533 --> 00:09:03.633 line:85%
Let's rotate it like this.

00:09:04.133 --> 00:09:04.733 line:85%
And we're already

00:09:04.733 --> 00:09:06.466 line:85%
getting a nice light here.

00:09:06.466 --> 00:09:08.066 line:85%
So a sunlight is often

00:09:08.066 --> 00:09:09.766 line:85%
used if you want hard shadows,

00:09:09.933 --> 00:09:11.766 line:85%
which often work well with products

00:09:11.766 --> 00:09:14.366 line:85%
that have a very strong flat color.

00:09:14.733 --> 00:09:15.633 line:85%
You will often see it in

00:09:15.633 --> 00:09:16.933 line:85%
like summertime commercials

00:09:17.133 --> 00:09:19.133 position:63% line:85%
like for sunscreen and things like that.

00:09:19.466 --> 00:09:20.333 line:85%
And you can also soften

00:09:20.333 --> 00:09:21.066 line:85%
the shadows if you want

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.433 line:85%
by increasing the angle

00:09:22.433 --> 00:09:24.133 line:85%
on the sunlight like this.

00:09:24.466 --> 00:09:25.166 line:85%
And for this to add

00:09:25.166 --> 00:09:26.399 line:85%
some more visual interest,

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:28.033 line:85%
I like to add some gobos,

00:09:28.299 --> 00:09:30.500 position:59% line:85%
which is texture for the light itself.

00:09:31.033 --> 00:09:32.799 line:85%
So let's first add a spotlight.

00:09:33.299 --> 00:09:34.633 line:85%
Let's make sure it's

00:09:34.633 --> 00:09:36.466 line:85%
lighting up this scene nicely

00:09:36.799 --> 00:09:38.333 line:85%
and let's increase it.

00:09:38.333 --> 00:09:39.100 line:85%
We probably have to

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.966 line:85%
increase the spot size.

00:09:41.366 --> 00:09:41.866 line:85%
That looks good.

00:09:42.266 --> 00:09:42.933 line:85%
And now make sure the

00:09:42.933 --> 00:09:44.066 line:85%
spotlight is selected,

00:09:44.066 --> 00:09:45.966 position:63% line:85%
going to use nodes and let's add a gobo.

00:09:46.333 --> 00:09:48.000 line:85%
So a gobo might look like

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.766 line:85%
this or this or this or this,

00:09:50.766 --> 00:09:51.600 line:85%
depending on what

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:52.299 line:85%
you're going to use it for.

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.299 position:56% line:85%
It basically applies this image as a

00:09:54.299 --> 00:09:55.299 line:85%
texture for the light.

00:09:55.666 --> 00:09:56.633 line:85%
So let's choose this one.

00:09:56.899 --> 00:09:57.733 line:85%
And all of this is in

00:09:57.733 --> 00:09:58.433 line:85%
the Patreon, of course.

00:09:58.799 --> 00:09:59.833 line:85%
Drag it into the shade

00:09:59.833 --> 00:10:01.233 line:85%
editor, connect it to color.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.533 position:59% line:85%
The shadows are a bit sharp right now.

00:10:03.933 --> 00:10:05.366 line:85%
So let's go into the light settings

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:07.066 line:85%
and let's increase the radius

00:10:07.066 --> 00:10:09.200 line:85%
slightly like this, I think.

00:10:09.533 --> 00:10:10.566 line:85%
And then just position the shadows

00:10:10.566 --> 00:10:11.899 line:85%
exactly how you want it to look.

00:10:12.166 --> 00:10:13.166 line:85%
All right, that's about it.

00:10:13.299 --> 00:10:13.866 line:85%
Thank you for watching

00:10:13.866 --> 00:10:14.899 line:85%
and see you in the next one.

00:10:15.066 --> 00:10:16.166 position:56% line:85%
You made it to the end of the video.

00:10:16.166 --> 00:10:17.600 position:63% line:85%
That means you're dedicated to learning.

00:10:17.833 --> 00:10:18.433 line:85%
And if you want to take

00:10:18.433 --> 00:10:19.433 line:85%
your blender skills seriously

00:10:19.533 --> 00:10:20.433 line:85%
or you just need

00:10:20.433 --> 00:10:21.333 line:85%
something to stay committed,

00:10:21.566 --> 00:10:22.366 line:85%
I just launched a

00:10:22.366 --> 00:10:23.866 line:85%
Patreon and at the third tier,

00:10:23.866 --> 00:10:24.899 line:85%
you can send me your blend file

00:10:24.899 --> 00:10:26.566 line:85%
and I will record a personal video

00:10:26.566 --> 00:10:27.533 line:85%
giving feedback on your

00:10:27.533 --> 00:10:28.966 line:85%
project every single month.

00:10:28.966 --> 00:10:29.566 line:85%
Link in the description.

00:10:29.899 --> 00:10:30.033 line:85%
All right.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:30.833 line:85%
Thanks for watching

00:10:30.833 --> 00:10:31.766 line:85%
and see you next time.

